WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:07.410
The Keki family has waited for this moment for more than three years.

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:12.100
Finally they can hold their daughter Hauwa in their arms again.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.000
"I'm so happy.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.150
Just happy and grateful to God."

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:24.760
They have a lot of catching-up to do.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:30.140
Hauwa's parents show her photos of the rest of the family - and she gets to see how everyone's changed.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:38.840
And then finally Hauwa gets to talk on the
phone with her siblings again.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.040
"They've constantly been asking about her.

00:00:45.049 --> 00:00:48.839
No day goes by when they haven't asked me:
'How is she?'

00:00:48.839 --> 00:00:51.059
'Does she get enough to eat?'

00:00:51.059 --> 00:00:52.079
'Where does she sleep?'

00:00:52.079 --> 00:00:53.589
'On a mattress?'

00:00:53.589 --> 00:00:55.460
'On leaves from the jungle?'

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:58.969
They really worried a lot about her and always asked about her.

00:00:58.969 --> 00:01:02.760
I then tried to calm them down and tell them that everything is okay and that she would

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.560
return one day."

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:10.219
Her father hopes that everybody will soon be able to live together again.

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:14.620
"If things remain peaceful now, she can return home.

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:16.090
Why shouldn't she?

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:19.980
She can return home and take her graduation
exam."

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:24.800
But that seems unlikely.

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:29.560
Last October, 23 girls were freed from the
militant group Boko Haram.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:33.249
The government still has the girls in its care in the capital.

00:01:33.249 --> 00:01:37.280
Some parents complain that they hardly get access to their own daughters.

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:46.579
A government spokesperson on Nigerian television offered this explanation.

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:52.260
"Ever since the most important thing for the country is that these girls are a security

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:54.380
interest in the fight against them.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:58.260
Who knows - among them maybe some of them have returned radicalized.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:03.120
And releasing them to the mainstream might
pose a danger itself to society."

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:11.420
Boko Haram recently released a video supposedly showing four of the kidnapped girls from Chibok.

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:15.880
In it they pledge loyalty to Boko Haram and refuse to return home.

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:21.980
Observers though are warning against placing
the girls under suspicion.

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:26.120
Instead they say, their families should be
brought in to play a greater role.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:35.820
"It is not acceptable that they should be
kept away from family, friends and relations

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:37.100
for so long.

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:40.650
I don't see any justification for that.

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:44.280
And the reasons given by government are not sufficient for me."

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:50.299
Hauwa's parents can only guess what she has gone through in the past three years.

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:56.020
All they hope for now, is some peace and quiet - and a return to somewhat of a normal life.

